# Every five minutes, publish a fresh snapshot for the Samba share. Ticket #30.
#
# Five minutes because the share is for looking at data afterwards, not for
# watching a game live: a stats session on the Mac can tolerate a snapshot a few
# minutes old, and a match that finishes is published within seconds anyway by
# the app itself (the match-completion hook in darts.api.play). Each run is one
# sqlite3 backup of a database measured in hundreds of kilobytes.
#
# Monotonic (OnUnitActiveSec) rather than wall-clock (OnCalendar), because the
# Pi has no battery-backed clock by default: until NTP syncs after a power cut
# the wall clock can be wrong, and a calendar timer would fire late, early or
# in a burst. "Five minutes since the last run" is correct whatever the clock
# says. AccuracySec is tightened from systemd's default of one minute, which
# would otherwise let each firing drift by up to a minute to coalesce wake-ups.

[Unit]
Description=Publish a darts snapshot every five minutes

[Timer]
OnBootSec=1min
OnUnitActiveSec=5min
AccuracySec=1s
Unit=darts-snapshot.service

[Install]
WantedBy=timers.target
